#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192478 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe4b690c-94a9-5a27-b0e8-5583ba6dba19" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Probability That a Random Variable Lies Within a Bounded Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "65070836-e061-5fec-ae8d-263ef0c32659" :question/math-academy-id "e-10839" :question/problem "Compute $P\\left( 1 \\lt   X \\lt 3 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n![](images/70/7059e7c4cb42e405342d34cd53ee7852f8abfffff2c3f54a95df30cdd44ef3c8.svg)" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a \\lt   X \\lt      b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<3) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{18}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}{\\int }_{1}^{3}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-x]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}([\\frac{1}{3}(3)^{3}-(3)]-[\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}-(1)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}([9-3]-[\\frac{1}{3}-1]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}(6+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}\\cdot \\frac{20}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192518 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e723a34-c6e1-5827-87ad-866cbaeef98c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Probability That a Random Variable Lies Within an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "d8425df8-1fb2-5f59-a034-2b30f14b9b4b" :question/math-academy-id "e-11036" :question/problem "Compute $P\\left(  X \\leq 3 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n![](images/b0/b083c72bc5c3bb6ea1a4f5036a57e5671c884d585def9e71f17a1ac72845d984.svg)" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a \\leq X \\leq  b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x \\lt  2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{2x}{45}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{45}\\,{x}^{2}]}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{45}({3}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{45}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192519 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "17408f35-ef57-5eb2-8cb6-3a946194d2d3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Probabilities With Piecewise PDFs"}] :question/id #uuid "4baa68f1-2f68-5df5-936a-aff56605ed8e" :question/math-academy-id "e-11038" :question/problem "Compute $P\\left( 2 \\leq          X \\leq          4 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n![](images/b4/b4da93ec01e058c31044ba7022c1e7109a7bacd4fd56c264df2ccfad5fbe2457.svg)" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a \\leq        X \\leq        b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 4) & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{9}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{4}(x-3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{18}{x}^{2}]}_{2}^{3}+{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-3x]}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}[{3}^{2}-{2}^{2}]+([\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{2}-3(4)]-[\\frac{1}{2}(3)^{2}-3(3)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{18}-4+\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406954 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e723a34-c6e1-5827-87ad-866cbaeef98c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Probability That a Random Variable Lies Within an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1faf4f36-14d4-5079-9551-250ad4e3cf1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406922} {:answer/id #uuid "38f73634-8e2d-501c-be17-972c94091082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406924} {:answer/id #uuid "6ff15794-2a8c-5b30-8865-ea10f20a2b20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406929} {:answer/id #uuid "7e67f1ca-b2f4-549e-815d-e10ef48f7256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406930} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4990e6-36da-5175-b799-75a15592dbaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc4990e6-36da-5175-b799-75a15592dbaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406938} :answer-field/id #uuid "092612b2-00fa-53f2-9670-ce20788500b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5e575cf-c390-5240-8f9f-2e2ff4fb107f" :question/math-academy-id "q-158308" :question/problem "Compute $P(X<1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}{x}^{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x<0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[1-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe4b690c-94a9-5a27-b0e8-5583ba6dba19" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Probability That a Random Variable Lies Within a Bounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83221410-a10d-5d0e-83cf-13c429350eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406931} {:answer/id #uuid "9abc5f15-a3ff-5d2b-9f5e-c96ef4c927ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406934} {:answer/id #uuid "9dda9524-0d12-5c08-9e65-638d5e2ca147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406935} {:answer/id #uuid "a4064c0a-6aa8-5917-b98d-ddc4782ccc34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406936} {:answer/id #uuid "fbf93cb8-21ed-52ed-b5b8-e67b0f616bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83221410-a10d-5d0e-83cf-13c429350eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406931} :answer-field/id #uuid "2819a566-5ed8-5910-94b3-ea46282d78d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "70b7a02c-90a1-5f9d-b1b7-a374071b4308" :question/math-academy-id "q-158352" :question/problem "Compute $P(0<X<1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}x(2-x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<X<1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{4}x(2-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}-{x}^{2}+2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{[-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}([-\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}+(1)^{2}]-[-\\frac{1}{3}(0)^{3}+(0)^{2}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}([-\\frac{1}{3}+1]-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "17408f35-ef57-5eb2-8cb6-3a946194d2d3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Probabilities With Piecewise PDFs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0adb4037-3d21-5577-98db-0520851d8ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406920} {:answer/id #uuid "0cdf27d3-c6d5-5df4-bb15-db45cd603f84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406921} {:answer/id #uuid "60218c40-e5fc-5799-88a4-377813f3a491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406927} {:answer/id #uuid "e92906ad-768d-5f7e-a293-b12fcc80bf8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406942} {:answer/id #uuid "ec9cd385-a95e-5534-93cc-032926c3dedc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0adb4037-3d21-5577-98db-0520851d8ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406920} :answer-field/id #uuid "9af9df66-4779-52c1-bd4c-a452e7989789" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "70e45506-8937-5eb7-832e-8c6f85a45f1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-158435" :question/problem "Compute $P(1<X<3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}({x}^{3}+x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}(x-2) & 2<x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<3) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{8}({x}^{3}+x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{8}(x-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{2}+\\frac{1}{8}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-2x]}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}([\\frac{1}{4}(2)^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{4}(1)^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2}])+\\frac{1}{8}([\\frac{1}{2}(3)^{2}-2(3)]-[\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}-2(2)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(6-\\frac{3}{4})+\\frac{1}{8}(\\frac{9}{2}-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(\\frac{21}{4})+\\frac{1}{8}(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{32}+\\frac{1}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278191 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "17408f35-ef57-5eb2-8cb6-3a946194d2d3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Probabilities With Piecewise PDFs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37a48388-2bab-577e-b3fc-ef5d85354f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275977} {:answer/id #uuid "52335667-e9ab-5c39-a40f-ac908fefa494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276216} {:answer/id #uuid "a514a2ee-a5b5-58f7-99f4-e1aefb256c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276973} {:answer/id #uuid "ba3431c2-fdec-5030-bef8-76e4881f3f81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277135} {:answer/id #uuid "c531fdd1-513c-5a30-9e26-04dd5456d859" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37a48388-2bab-577e-b3fc-ef5d85354f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275977} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5b0873d-3a7a-5181-858a-c7d1ba8a1bad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278019}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a416229-b58d-58b1-a133-9fc7c0c01068" :question/math-academy-id "q-158436" :question/problem "Compute $P(0\\le X\\le 2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}x(x+1),\\, & 0\\le x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}x & 1\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{5}x(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{6}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{5}({x}^{2}+x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{6}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1}+{[\\frac{1}{12}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}([\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{3}(0)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}])+\\frac{1}{12}[{2}^{2}-{1}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}(\\frac{5}{6})+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e723a34-c6e1-5827-87ad-866cbaeef98c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Probability That a Random Variable Lies Within an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37263c1d-3a90-5cbf-a914-8e3374163496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406923} {:answer/id #uuid "39e8336e-8823-5190-8258-986854592e5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406925} {:answer/id #uuid "a4262a2b-8e1a-56af-8617-c7da79b0d0c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406937} {:answer/id #uuid "ceff823a-381d-55c5-8f08-28d5ad75ecd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406939} {:answer/id #uuid "e1005a2d-863c-5e8e-9016-26d842f75de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4262a2b-8e1a-56af-8617-c7da79b0d0c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406937} :answer-field/id #uuid "0429e265-c0ef-5ef4-977e-8cd0e19add5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406945}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71e34130-ba0f-56bf-99cf-bcd67e888e34" :question/math-academy-id "q-158464" :question/problem "Compute $P(X>7)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{36}x,\\, & 3\\le x\\le 9, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x>9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>7) & ={\\int }_{7}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{7}^{9}\\frac{1}{36}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{72}{x}^{2}]}_{7}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{72}({9}^{2}-{7}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{72}(81-49) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{72} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe4b690c-94a9-5a27-b0e8-5583ba6dba19" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Probability That a Random Variable Lies Within a Bounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b4c000b-c921-5509-a96b-cb9f0d93c9ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406926} {:answer/id #uuid "670ba1f9-ed3f-5406-a924-34d394e42af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406928} {:answer/id #uuid "8f9616d5-ee83-53e1-8dc5-492827d8a46f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406932} {:answer/id #uuid "90f92edc-d0c5-5a32-ba22-e172277f28a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406933} {:answer/id #uuid "e5c1b6f1-8629-5f1d-8828-dbc4c3ad5ba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90f92edc-d0c5-5a32-ba22-e172277f28a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406933} :answer-field/id #uuid "97997922-270d-5956-b157-409ccbb997d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "77d8a3b9-ab3f-5af1-ac16-cd6ceeb35611" :question/math-academy-id "q-87213" :question/problem "Compute $P(1<X\\le 5)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{18}x,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X\\le 5) & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{18}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{36}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
